Rule 1 (dimension of array to integrate must be at least 1)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 2 (axis of integration must be within valid range for the input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= v_2 + ndim(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 3 (spacing dx must be non-zero)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≠ 0
>>
Rule 4 (input tensor y must have a numeric dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 5 (if sample points x are provided, its shape must match y's shape, or it must be 1D with size matching y's shape along the integration axis)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= v_3 + ndim(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ v_3 < ndim(v_1) ∧ (if ndim(v_2) = 1 then shape(v_2, 0) = shape(v_1, if v_3 < 0 then v_3 + ndim(v_1) else v_3) else (ndim(v_2) = ndim(v_1) ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, i))))
>>
Rule 9 (spacing dx must be a 0D or 1D tensor if it is a tensor)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≤ 1
>>
Rule 12 (size of the integration dimension must be at least 2 to apply the trapezoidal rule)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= shape(v_1, if v_2 < 0 then v_2 + ndim(v_1) else v_2) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 13 (dimensionality of sample points x must not exceed that of y)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 14 (axis of integration must be within valid range)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= v_2 ≥ 0 - ndim(v_1) ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 15 (sample points x must have a real-valued numeric dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 16 (if sample points x is 1D, its length must be at least 2)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 2
